TWO LICENCES, AND WHICH APPLIES TO WHAT
=======================================

PUBLIC DOMAIN (CC0 1.0 Universal)
---------------------------------
    spec/           the specification
    registry/       jurisdictions, corpora and kinds
    conformance/    the conformance corpus
    the identifier strings themselves
    the published concordance (concordance.jsonl.gz)

    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

CC0 is a waiver, not a licence. Section 2 of the legal code has the Affirmer
"overtly, fully, permanently, irrevocably and unconditionally waive, abandon,
and surrender" the rights in the work. Surrendered rights cannot be reclaimed by
a later owner of the company, because there is nothing left to inherit. This is
deliberate and permanent.

An identifier nobody can charge for is the whole point. Charging for the number
is the CUSIP path: a licence fee for storing the number in your own database, an
antitrust complaint alleging group boycott, and a federal statute now requiring
agencies to use non-proprietary identifiers where practicable.


